// Deposit models (v2 §13.2): where and in what shape each resource occurs. The world generator
// places real bodies — veins, seams, nodule bands, placers, disseminated ore bodies, crusts,
// pipes, bog ores, evaporites and lava flows — in the listed provinces, inside the host rocks
// (when listed), and marks shallow ones at the surface with their indicators.
//
// Conditions: any of the places (river, lake, wetland) must hold when one is listed, and all the
// others (arid, humid, warm, cold, volcano = near a volcano, granite = near a granite body;
// placers need the granite within a few hundred metres upstream).
// Depths are real metres below the local surface (deep bodies scale with the world's vertical
// scale); sizes, thicknesses and extents are metres (a block is a metre). Grade is the mass
// fraction of the resource in the body; most rock is just rock. Frequency is bodies per km² of
// suitable ground in the world. Era is the first technological era that uses the resource.
